A||||5||black86gt||Gutting the Cat.
Z||000000||black86gt||03-14-99||05:46 PM||||Ok I have been told by gutting the cat I will get an extra 5hp form it.  Thats sounds nice.  I would like to know about the procedure to gut it or/also remove it.  Thanks again.
Z||000001||raceknb||03-18-99||07:26 PM||||Your not going to find many people willing to answer a question like that here.  Federal Law prohibits the removal or modification of ANY factory insatlled emission control device.  Failure to comply CAN result in a fine of up to $2500 and 6 months in Jail.  No that that is out of the way.  Gutting the cat will require splitiing the tac welds located along the sides of the casing.  removing the inner material can then take place.  Then carefully re-weld the 2 halves back into place and re-install.  You would be better to just have a test pipe built at your local speed shop and switch them out in the comfort of you driveway.  Good luck...thats lots of work for 5 hp.<br>
Z||000002||Pretender||04-05-99||02:08 AM||||Gutting the cat, the easyiest wat to do it is by running a solid pipe through the center knocking out all the crud....it's alot easier just to get a straight pipe(not from the fiero store unless you wanna pay quadrouple the price...it's completely straight and any napa/parts america/westernauto carries it....It is against the law in any state that requires emisions testing....but here in pennsylvania everybody guts the cat/ removes the smog pump...goodluck
Z||000003||theogre||04-05-99||11:52 PM||||Pretender, others,<p>yeah, you can gut the cat. You might want to be aware that emisions laws are ever changing. PA for example won sortof against the EPA. In the end the EPA will likely win.<p>In DE, and MD, you'd not get away with a bad cat. MD has a whole seperate emissions testing from it's inspection process. DE looks under the car.... they will fail a car with a removed cat, even if it passes emisions. DE even tests your gas tank, and gas cap. Gas caps nearly all years, gas tanks after late 80's) These kinds of things are coming for nearly ALL states in the contiguous 48.
Z||000004||PaUL||04-07-99||06:36 PM||||I completely removed my cat and replaced it with a strait pipe. Here in Hawaii we are free to pollute our pristine air as much as we want. The only inspection is a yearly safety check where the lights, horn, brakes, and tires are checked, they never even look at your engine of emissions control devices.
Z||000005||theogre||04-07-99||08:17 PM||||lucky you. in most eastern states now they physically look, as well as put a probe in the pipe.
